data: {"id":"chatcmpl-8101e3b7-71fd-4376-a0ac-8c56b2757e28","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1790744766,"model":"capitoline-judge-sol6","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"content":"RF2 stores two copies of each piece of data on different nodes. If one node fails in a three-node cluster, data that had a copy on that node is left with **one surviving copy**; data whose copies were on the other two nodes remains at RF2. The surviving nodes retain quorum, so the cluster can continue serving data.\n\nThe cluster can automatically copy the affected data between the two surviving nodes and restore two copies, provided they have enough free storage. Until that rebuild finishes, affected data has no backup copy. Even after it finishes, the cluster has not regained its normal failure tolerance: another node failure would break quorum and interrupt cluster operation. Repairing or replacing the failed node restores the three-node configuration."},"finish_reason":null}]}

